## Intended use

Generate fictional first names in the style of French literature characters:

```python
from onomatron.serialize import load_bundle_from_hub

net, config = load_bundle_from_hub("{{ model_repo }}")
print(net.sample(n=20, seed=42))
```

or from the command line, from this repo's root:

```bash
python generate.py --bundle . --n 20 --seed 42
```

### Out-of-scope use

Not a model of language in general: no semantics, no grammar beyond character
statistics, French literary names only. Do not use it to name real persons or
for any decision about individuals.

## Training data

[{{ dataset_repo }}](https://huggingface.co/datasets/{{ dataset_repo }}) — one
sanitized name per line (see its card for full provenance and per-source
licenses).

## Training procedure

1. Hyperparameter tuning with **Optuna** (TPE sampler + ASHA pruning,
   objective = val NLL, persistent SQLite studies); every trial tracked in
   **MLflow**.
2. Final retraining for `final_steps` = {{ run.params.get("final_steps") }} steps
   with the best params: AdamW (lr = `{{ run.params.get("lr") }}`,
   weight_decay = `{{ run.params.get("weight_decay") }}`,
   clip_grad = `{{ run.params.get("clip_grad") }}`,
   batch_size = {{ run.params.get("batch_size") }}), seed = {{ seed }},
   device = {{ device }}, early stopping (patience = {{ run.params.get("patience") }}).

## Evaluation

Protocol: names are split **by name** (never by n-gram, to avoid leakage
between correlated n-grams of the same name) into train/val/test = 80/10/10
with a fixed seed; the test split is touched exactly once, in the final
evaluation. Inference speed is measured on CPU.

